From: Amit Seth <sudarshanchakraindia@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 01:11:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix admin-uploaded marketing material failing to open, and
 enable WhatsApp file sharing

getDownloadURL() returns an already percent-encoded URL. Passing it through
encodeURI() escaped the '%' a second time (%2F -> %252F), so every material
uploaded via partner-admin.html produced a storage URL pointing at an object
name that does not exist. The Open link and the card thumbnails both broke;
partner-admin.html was unaffected because it uses the raw URL.

- use escapeHtml() instead of encodeURI() at all five URL-into-HTML sites
- split the file fetch out of shareFileOrLink() so both the share and the new
  download path can reuse it
- add a labelled WhatsApp button and a download fallback to each material card
- share the partner's own referral link as the message text rather than the
  long storage URL
- add cors.json; the bucket needs it before a cross-origin fetch of a poster
  can succeed, which is what blocks attaching the file to WhatsApp

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UqsceAiDiQwwUxeJf2es32
